Write a solution to find the IDs of the users who visited without making any transactions and the number of times they made these types of visits.

Return the result table sorted in any order.
# Write your MySQL query statement below
SELECT v.customer_id, SUM(t.transaction_id IS NULL) as count_no_trans 
FROM Visits v LEFT JOIN Transactions t on v.visit_id = t.visit_id
#LEFT JOIN gives all the rows from visits. If visit id is not present in Transactions table then all cols from transaction table is filled as null. 
#The agg function SUM adds up total number of null values and returns just one value. Since we need value per customer, we add GROUP BY and then the condition of that value being greater than 0. 
GROUP BY v.customer_id
HAVING count_no_trans >0;
